The decision as to whether a complaint or First Information Report should be quashed on the ground that the offender and victim have settled the dispute, revolves ultimately on the facts and circumstances of each case and no exhaustive elaboration of principles can be formulated;
Aman Yadav And Others vs State Of U.P. And Another on 19 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/80949120/
2 16.6.

Criminal cases involving offences which arise from commercial, financial,
mercantile, partnership or similar transactions with an essentially civil flavour may in appropriate situations fall for quashing where parties have settled the dispute;
16.9.
